{
  "dom_id": "step-e7860",
  "name": "Example: Representing Combined Stretches Using Functions",
  "problem": "What function represents the combined stretch of factor $4$ in the $x$-direction and factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ in the $y$-direction?",
  "worked_solution": "- A stretch in the $x$-direction of factor $4$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto (4x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch in the $y$-direction of factor $\\dfrac 1 4$ can be represented by the function \n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)\\mapsto \\left(4x,\\dfrac 1 4y\\right).\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
